From: u6d1cd0a71e6148df at groups.google.com (Karl Ove Hufthammer)
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 11:57:10 +0000
Subject: Strange diagonals with plotmatrix for data frames with non-numeric variables
Message-ID: <pRREYO-Jx6Q.oYabxGYjfPQJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/pRREYO-Jx6Q/m/oYabxGYjfPQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Compare the output of

plotmatrix(iris[,1:4])

with the output of

plotmatrix(iris)

The diagonal panels should be identical for the four first variables,
but they aren’t. In the ‘plotmatrix(iris)’ example they show some
strange curves, while in the ‘plotmatrix(iris[,1:4])’ example they
(correctly) show density estimates.

--
Karl Ove Hufthammer

